{"id":"word:hebrew:H2891","type":"word","title":"טָהֵר","subtitle":"H2891 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to be pure (physical sound, clear, unadulterated; Levitically, uncontaminated; morally, innocent or holy)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to טָהֵר (H2891) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 95 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"טָהֵר (ṭâhêr) means to be pure (physical sound, clear, unadulterated; Levitically, uncontaminated; morally, innocent or holy) First listed occurrence: 2Chr 29 15."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"טָהֵר","transliteration":"ṭâhêr","pronunciation":"taw-hare'","strong":"H2891","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2891","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וְ/טָהֵֽר","הַ/מִּטַּהֵ֖ר","וְ/טִהַ֤ר","וּ/טְהָֽר","וּ/טְהַרְתֶּ֑ם"],"morphs":[["HC/Vqq3ms",13],["HTd/Vtrmsa",11],["HC/Vpq3ms/Sp3ms",6],["HR/Vpc",5],["HVqi3ms",5],["HC/Vpq3ms",5],["HVtp3cp",2],["HC/Vqv2ms",2],["HVqi2fs",2],["HC/Vqq2mp",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to be pure (physical sound, clear, unadulterated; Levitically, uncontaminated; morally, innocent or holy)","usage":"be (make, make self, pronounce) clean, cleanse (self), purge, purify(-ier, self).","full":"H2891. taher טָהֵר verb be clean, pure (Arabic , id. ; Late Hebrew id. , Pi`el make or declare ceremonially clean ; Aramaic טְהַר emptiness , טִיהֲרָא brightness ; Sabean טהר Hal 682 ; Ethiopic purify, wash oneself with water ) — Qal Perfect ׳ט Lev 11:32 12 t.; 3 feminine singular טָֽהֲרָה 12:7 ; 15:28 ; טָהֵ֑רָה 12:8 etc., + 5 t. Perfect; Imperfect יִטְהַר 15:13 ; Job 4:17 etc., + 9 t. Imperfect; Imperative טְהָ֑ר 2Kin 5:10 , 13 ; &#8212; 1 be clean , i.e. (miraculously) freed from leprosy by washing in the Jordan 2Kin 5:10 , 12 , 13 , 14 . 2 be clean ceremonially (only H P), Lev 15:13 , 28 (twice in verse) (P), 22:4 (H); by washing with water, the flesh 22:7 (H); garments 13:6 , 34 , 58 ; Num 31:24 (all P); both flesh and garments Lev 17:5 (H), 14:8-9 , 15:13 ; Num 19:19 (all P); other articles Lev 11:32 (P); passing things through the fire Num 31:23 (P); offering sin-offerings Lev 12:7-8 , 14:20 (P); by the ceremony of the two birds 14:53 (P); by ashes of red heifer Num 19:12 (twice in verse) (P). 3 be clean morally , of people, made clean by ׳י s scattering clean water upon them Ezek 36:25 ; of Jerusalem, specifically made clean from idolatry, under figure of adultery Jer 13:27 ; also followed by מִן Ezek 24:13 (twice in verse) (purification by ׳י ); made clean מִכָּלחַֿטּאֹתֵיכֶם Lev 16:30 (P; by the sin-offering of the atonement day); also of the individual, be clean מֵחַטָּאוֺת Prov 20:9 (|| זכה ); become clean by use of hyssop Psa 51:9 (|| אַלְבִּין ); more Generally יִטְהַרגָּֿ֑בֶר אִםמֵֿעשֵֹׁהוּ Job 4:17 shall a man be more pure than his maker ? (|| יִצְדָּ֑ק ). Pi`el Perfect טִהַר Lev 13:3-4 t.; suffix טִהֲרוֺ 13:6 5 t.; 2 masculine singular טִהַרְתָּ Num 8:6 , 15 etc. + 7 t. Perfect; Imperfect ; יְטַהֵר 2Chr 34:5 etc. + 4 t. Imperfect; Imperative suffix טַהֲרֵנִי Psa 51:4 ; Infinitive construct טַהֵר Ezek 39:12 5 t.; suffix טַהֲרִי 36:33 etc. + 4 t. Infinitive; Participle מְטַחֵר Lev 14:11 ; Mal 3:3 ; &#8212; chiefly P; 1 cleanse, purify: a. physically , metals from dross Mal 3:3 ; land from corpses Ezek 39:12 , 14 , 16 ; heavens from clouds Job 37:21 ; temple from unclean things 2Chr 29:15-16 , 18 ; land and city from Asherim and images 34:3 , 5 , 8 ; store-chambers of temple from household stuff Neh 13:9 ; priesthood by exclusion of alien blood 13:30 . b. ceremonially , the altar of incense by the blood of the annual sin-offering Lev 16:19 (P); the people, gates, and wall (by some undefined ceremony) Neh 12:30 ; the altar of the court by the blood of sin-offerings Ezek 43:26 ; of consecration of Levites by חטאת מֵי Num 8:6-7 , (P), and חטאת 8:15 , 21 (P). c. morally Lev 16:30 (P), Ezek 37:23 ; Mal 3:3 ; מֵחַטָּאֹת Psa 51:4 ; מֵעונ(ותׅ Jer 33:8 ; Ezek 36:33 ; מִטּמא(ו)ת 24:13 ; 36:25 . 2 pronounce clean , ceremonially Lev 13:6 ; 13:13 ; 13:17 ; 13:23 ; Leviticus 12:28; 13:34 , 37 , 59 ; 14:7 , 48 (all P). 3 perform the ceremony of cleansing Lev 14:11 (P). Pu`al Perfect 3masculine singular טֹהַר 1Sam 20:26 (so. read for ᵐ5 טהור ᵑ0 We Dr, he is not clean, because he hath not been cleansed ); Participle מְטֹהָרָה לֹא אֶרֶץ a land not cleansed Ezek 22:24 (but ᵐ5 Hi Ew Co SS read a land not rained upon , see מטר ). Hithpa`el Perfect 3plural הִטָּֽהֲרוּ Ezra 6:20 ; הִטֶּהָ֑רוּ (Kö i. 271 ) 2Chr 30:18 ; Num 8:7 ; 1 plural הִטַּהַרְנוּ Josh 22:17 ; Imperfect יִטָּֽהֲרוּ Neh 12:30 ; Imperative הִטָּֽהֲרוּ Gen 35:2 ; Participle מִטַּהֵר Lev 14:7 11 t.; plural מִטַּהֲרִים Neh 13:22 ; Isa 66:17 ; &#8212; reflexive: 1 purify oneself: a. ceremonially , especially in preparation for sacred duties Gen 35:2 (R), Num 8:7 ; 2Chr 30:18 ; Ezra 6:20 ; Neh 13:22 ; also for heathen mysteries Isa 66:17 ; of purifying priests, people, and wall Neh 12:30 (compare Pi`el 1 b ). b. morally Josh 22:17 (P). 2 present oneself for purification , only participle הַמִּטַּהֵר the candidate for purification Lev 14:4 , 7 , 8 , 11 , 14 , 17 , 18 , 19 , 25 , 28 , 29, 31 (P).","rootNote":"a primitive root; properly, to be bright; i.e. (by implication)","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Chr 29 15","keyReferences":["2Chr 29 15","2Chr 29 16","2Chr 29 18","2Chr 30 18","2Chr 34 3","2Chr 34 5","2Chr 34 8","2Kgs 5 10"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":95,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Chr 29 15","book":"2Chr","chapter":29,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/טַהֵ֖ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vpc"},{"reference":"2Chr 29 16","book":"2Chr","chapter":29,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/טַהֵר֒","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vpc"},{"reference":"2Chr 29 18","book":"2Chr","chapter":29,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":